-- EXPECT-ERROR: calls `panic`, which can panic
-- Capabilities widening, Task 4 -- `cap no_panic` (`check_no_panic_module`,
-- `typecheck.ml:6116-6193`), the REJECT side for the most direct panic
-- surface: an explicit call to `panic`. `panic` is a member of
-- `panic_surface_direct` (`typecheck.ml:6035-6041`) -- the syntactic
-- call-collector `calls_in_expr` (`:6085-6114`) finds `fail`'s body calls
-- `panic`, `is_direct_panic_site` (`:6135-6138`) matches it directly (no
-- fixpoint/transitive step needed), and `check_no_panic_module` reports an
-- ERROR at the call site: `` `fail` in `mod Guarded` (declared `cap
-- no_panic`) calls `panic`, which can panic. `` See core-march-types.md
-- §2.8.11.
mod Guarded do
  cap no_panic

  fn fail() : Int do
    panic("boom")
  end
end
